    "title": "News From Around the Web",
    "text": "• Federal prosecutors issued grand jury subpoenas to Minnesota officials, including Gov. Tim Walz and Attorney General Keith Ellison, as part of an investigation into potential obstruction of law enforcement during an immigration operation.\n• Donald Trump criticized Supreme Court justices regarding cases on transgender athletes in women's sports, suggesting they should lose credibility.\n• Donald Trump's proposed \"Board of Peace\" faces pushback, with its mandate focusing on promoting stability and peace in conflict zones, but not specifically mentioning Gaza.\n• Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent stated Americans could receive larger tax refunds due to Donald Trump's economic policies.\n• Amazon is ending its delivery partnership with the United States Postal Service after a reported $9.5 billion loss for USPS.\n• A former Trump administration Education Department official exposed alleged federal student aid fraud in certain states.\n• The House Oversight Committee will vote on holding Bill and Hillary Clinton in contempt for refusing to appear before the committee regarding the Jeffrey Epstein investigation.\n• An Iranian military official warned Donald Trump of severe consequences if any harm comes to Iran's Supreme Leader.\n• An explosives expert testified that the pipe devices found on Capitol Hill on January 6, 2021, were not capable of exploding.\n• Donald Trump signed an executive order barring Wall Street investors from buying single-family homes.",
